Q: Gaussian in pascal A: <p>The <code>rand</code> function is in the [0, 1) interval (written as chained comparison: 0 ≤ <code>rand</code> &lt; 1)</p>
<ul>
<li>so 2.0 × <code>rand</code> − 1.0 is in the [−1, 1) interval</li>
<li>so <code>x1</code> and <code>x2</code> are in [−1, 1) interval</li>
<li>so <code>w := x1 * x1 + x2 * x2</code> is in the [0, 2) interval</li>
</ul>
<p>and in <code>sqrt( -2.0 * ln( w ) / w )</code> the <code>w</code> is positive</p>
<ul>
<li>so the natural logarithm <code>ln(w)</code> should be negative</li>
<li>so <code>w</code> should be in the (0, 1) interval</li>
<li>so that the loop should not exit <code>until (w &gt; 0.0) and (w &lt; 1.0);</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Working sample code (using SCAR Divi 3.41.00):</p>
<pre class="lang-pascal prettyprint-override"><code>program New;

 var hgauss : boolean;
 var ngauss : double;

  function gauss() : double;
  var x1, x2, w : double;
  begin
    if hgauss then
    begin
      result := ngauss;
      hgauss := false;
    end else
    begin
      repeat
        x1 := 2.0 * rand() - 1.0;
        x2 := 2.0 * rand() - 1.0;
        w := x1 * x1 + x2 * x2;
      until (w &gt; 0.0) and (w &lt; 1.0);
      w := sqrt( -2.0 * ln( w ) / w );
      result := x1 * w;
      ngauss := x2 * w;
      hgauss := true;
    end;
  end;

begin
  writeln( gauss() );
  writeln( gauss() );
end.
</code></pre>

Q: Reloading an image without changing the URL A: <p>I have a horrible contraption that works:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function do_refresh(images) {
    images.forEach(
        (image) =&gt;
            {
                fetch(image.url)
                    .then((response) =&gt;
                        {
                            if(!response.ok)
                            {
                                throw Error();
                            }
                            return response.blob();
                        })
                    .then((blob) =&gt;
                        {
                            image.element.src = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
                        })
                    .catch((error) =&gt; { });
            });
}

function start_refresh() {
    var images = Array.from(document.getElementsByTagName('img'))
        .map((image) =&gt;
            {
                return { element: image, url: image.src };
            });
    setInterval(() =&gt; { do_refresh(images); }, 300000);
}
</code></pre>
<p>Some code was blatantly stolen from <a href="https://medium.com/@a1guy/fetching-and-displaying-images-in-javascript-9848bc13f60e" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a>.</p>
<p>Credit goes to @YounisYousaf and @ArianaRose for pointing the right way.</p>

Q: Jetpack compose - How to do popBackStack with arguments? A: <h2>My solution for popBack with arguments</h2>
<p>Create a shared ViewModel once at the NavHost level and pass the same instance to nested navigation graphs.</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>@HiltViewModel
class NavHostViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val savedStateHandle: SavedStateHandle
) : ViewModel() {
    val argumentState =
        savedStateHandle.getStateFlow&lt;String?&gt;(
            PROCESSED_REQUEST_ID,
            null
        )

    fun setArgument(value: String) {
        savedStateHandle[PROCESSED_REQUEST_ID] = value
    }

    fun consumeResult(value: String) {
        if (resultState.value == value) {
            savedStateHandle[RESULT_KEY] = null
        }
    }

    private companion object {
        const val PROCESSED_REQUEST_ID =
            &quot;processed_z_rodziny_request_id&quot;
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Usage in NavHost:</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>@Composable
fun AppNavHost(
    navController: NavHostController,
    viewModel: NavHostViewModel = hiltViewModel(),
) {
    NavHost(
        navController = navController,
        startDestination = Route.ScreenA
    ) {
        composable&lt;Route.ScreenA&gt; { screenAEntry -&gt;
            val detailsViewModel: DetailsViewModel =
                hiltViewModel(screenAEntry)

            val result by
                viewModel.resultState.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()

            LaunchedEffect(result) {
                // Retrieve and consume the navigation result
                val value = result
                    ?: return@LaunchedEffect

                detailsViewModel.onResultReceived(value)
                viewModel.consumeResult(value)
            }

            ScreenA(
                viewModel = detailsViewModel
            )
        }

        composable&lt;Route.ScreenB&gt; {
            ScreenB(
                onBackWithResult = { result -&gt;
                // Pass a result back to the previous destination
                    viewModel.setResult(result) 
                    navController.popBackStack()
                }
            )
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
